update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin making the dressing by combining all the dressing ingredients in a small bowl and seasoning to perfection before setting aside.
2. In a separate bowl, roughly mash together the avocado flesh, lemon juice and yoghurt.
3. Be careful not to make the mixture too smooth, as you want it to have a chunky texture.
4. Divide the avocado mixture between the slices of toasted rye bread.
5. Sprinkle over a pinch of cayenne pepper to add a touch of heat and colour before layering the smoked salmon and cucumber ribbons on top.
6. Finish by placing a small handful of watercress on top of the salmon and drizzling over the dressing.
7. To stop a half-eaten avocado going brown.
8. Brush the avocado with lemon juice; the citric acid in the juice will keep browning at bay.
9. Store in an airtight container to get as much protection as possible.$r$ where name=$r$Avocado on toast with smoked salmon$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
