update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Sauté the onion and garlic in oil for 3 to 5 minutes until soft.
2. Add the green onions, cumin, and mushrooms and cook for a further 5 minutes, until mushrooms are cooked.
3. At this point if the mix becomes very dry, you can add a little more oil.
4. Once cooked set aside Meanwhile mash the beans in a large bowl, or alternatively you can pulse them in a food processor.
5. To the mashed beans add the onion and mushroom mix along with the parsley, salt, and pepper, combine well.
6. Shape the mixture into patties one inch thick.
7. If you make them too thin, they are likely to break up, too thick, and they will be difficult to cook evenly all the way through.
8. Heat about two tablespoons of oil over a medium heat and cook each patty until done, this should take about 3 minutes each side.
9. These are super tasty cooked on a griddle pan!$r$ where name=$r$Vegan Mushroom Bean Burger (v)$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Bring a wok or deep saucepan to medium-high heat and add the oil, chillies, lemongrass and ginger.
