12. Serve with bowls of steaming, fluffy jasmine rice.$r$ where name=$r$Vegan Thai green Curry (v)$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin by preheating your grill to a high temperature.
2. Meanwhile, in an ovenproof frying pan sauté the onions for 10 minutes until they have softened.
3. Add the honey to the pan and leave to bubble for 2 minutes allowing the onions to caramelise.
4. As the onions caramelise, beat the eggs before adding them to the pan.
5. Cook for 5 minutes until the eggs have almost set before crumbling goat’s cheese over the top.
6. Place the frittata under the hot grill and cook until a delicious layer of melted cheese has formed on top and the eggs have firmly set.
7. As the frittata cooks, combine together the rocket and beetroot in a large bowl and dress with lemon juice for some extra zing.
8. To serve, cut the frittata into quarters and serve with the beetroot salad for some added freshness.
9. If you’re not a fan of honey (or Canadian) you can easily switch out the honey for maple syrup.$r$ where name=$r$Goat’s Cheese & caramelised Onion frittata$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Put the onion, garlic, butter and spices in a microwaveable container, stir, then heat in the microwave on high for 30-40 seconds.
2. Allow to stand for 1 min, then add the chopped tomatoes, beans, stock cube and chocolate.
3. Cover with microwaveable cling film and pierce 3 times.
4. Place some kitchen paper on your microwave turntable, put the container on top and cook for 2 mins on high.
5. Stir well and leave to stand for a further minute.
6. If your chilli starts to dry out, add some of the reserved tomato juice, but bear in mind that it won’t reduce as much in the microwave as it would on the hob.
7. Cover and cook on medium for a further 2 minutes.
8. Give it a good stir and allow to stand for 1 minute before serving topped with soured cream and coriander or your favourite Mexican topping if desired$r$ where name=$r$15 Minute Beef Chilli$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by steaming the carrot over boiling water or in the microwave.
2. Meanwhile, heat the coconut oil in a large frying pan on medium heat.
3. Add the all spice, garlic, and coconut milk, stirring constantly.
4. Place the fish in the frying pan, cover and cook for 10-12 minutes.
5. Serve fish with carrots and fresh parsley.$r$ where name=$r$Coconut Fish$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Add corn and courgette to a medium sized bowl and toss with olive oil, lime juice, salt & cracked pepper.
2. Transfer to a serving plate and arrange with prosciutto cigars and chunks of persian feta.$r$ where name=$r$Prosciutto, Corn & Courgette Plate$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Bring a large frying pan to high heat, add olive oil and cook aubergine for 12-15 minutes or until very soft.
2. After 15 minutes, add the spice mix, stir to coat and cook for another 5 minutes.
3. Meanwhile, prepare the tortillas by placing them in the microwave for 30 seconds.
4. Next, layer them with lettuce, tomato, cucumber and avocado.
5. Top with aubergine, salsa and fresh coriander.
6. Serve immediately.$r$ where name=$r$Aubergine Tortillas$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Heat the olive oil in a large pan over a medium heat, sauté the garlic, onion, celery, carrots and peppers for a few minutes until softened.
2. Stir in the cumin, chilli powder, salt and pepper.
3. Next, add in the chopped tomatoes, kidney beans, lentils, soy mince and vegetable stock and simmer for a further 25 minutes.
4. Serve with some fluffy basmati rice, topped with fresh torn coriander and a squeeze of lime juice.
5. This recipe freezes well and will also keep for up to 4 days refrigerated.$r$ where name=$r$Chilli Sin Carne (v)$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Bring a saucepan of water to the boil over a medium heat and add the quinoa.
2. Cover and let the quinoa simmer for 10 to 15 minutes until the water is completely absorbed and the quinoa is fluffy.
3. Drain the quinoa and transfer to a bowl to cool.
4. Once the quinoa has cooled, stir in the avocado, tomato, salmon and rocket making sure that it is well mixed.
5. To make the dressing, combine the yoghurt, feta cheese and oregano in a small bowl.
6. To serve, add a dollop of yoghurt dressing on of the quinoa and enjoy.
7. Quinoa is gluten-free, high in protein and one of the few plant foods that contain sufficient amounts of all nine essential amino acids.
8. It is also high in fibre, magnesium, B vitamins, iron, potassium, calcium, phosphorus, vitamin E and various beneficial antioxidants.$r$ where name=$r$Salmon Quinoa Bowl$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Place the chicken breasts, 1 at a time, in a Ziploc bag and pound the chicken to an even thickness, being careful not to puncture the bag.
2. Place all the chicken back in the bag when finished.
3. Next, combine the soy sauce, apple sauce, onion, ginger, garlic, oil, bourbon, BBQ sauce, vinegar, brown sugar and red pepper flakes together in a small bowl.
4. Reserve and refrigerate 80ml of the marinade and transfer the remainder to the Ziploc bag with the chicken.
5. Marinate in your refrigerator for at least 30 minutes or overnight if possible.
6. Preheat your grill pan over medium high heat.
7. Grill the chicken for 4 minutes per side, or until chicken is cooked through.
8. Discard the remaining marinade.
9. Transfer the chicken to a plate, tent with foil and allow to rest while you make the sauce.
10. Pour the reserved marinade in a small pan.
11. Add the chicken broth and bring to a boil over medium high heat.
12. Then reduce the heat to medium until sauce has thickened slightly.
13. Slice chicken breasts, top with the sauce, garnish with the spring onions and serve.$r$ where name=$r$Grilled Bourbon Chicken$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by cooking ravioli according to packet instructions.
2. Drain and set aside.
3. In a separate pan, add the tuna, passata, oregano, Italian herbs and chilli flakes.
4. Cook stirring constantly for 4-5 minutes.
5. Add the cooked ravioli to the pan and stir through to heat for 2 minutes.
6. Transfer to 3 bowls and season with salt & cracked pepper.$r$ where name=$r$Tuna Ravioli$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by cooking the rice according to packet instructions.
2. Meanwhile, bring a large wok to medium high heat, add coconut oil and onion and cook for 4-5 minutes or until onion has softened.
3. Next, add the garlic and vegetables and cook for another five minutes.
4. Meanwhile, crack the eggs into a small bowl and whisk.
5. Transfer the eggs to a medium sized fry pan and cook like an omelette.
6. Remove from the pan, chop into bite sized pieces and add to the wok.
7. Add the pulled roast chicken, sriracha and tamari and heat through.
8. Divide into 4 bowls and serve hot.$r$ where name=$r$Roast Chicken Fried Rice$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by threading the lamb, onion, bell pepper and courgette onto 12 skewers and place on a long plate or shallow dish.
2. Mix together the garlic, oregano and olive oil.
3. Pour over the skewers and place them in the fridge to marinate for 30 minutes.
4. Bring a grill plate to high heat and cook skewers for about 10 minutes, or until cooked to your liking, making sure you rotate often to ensure all sides are cooked.
5. Serve with a simple Greek salad.$r$ where name=$r$Mediterranean Lamb Skewers$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by preheating oven to 175c/350f/Gas 4.
2. Line a baking tray with baking paper.
3. In a large bowl, mix together the garlic, olive oil, lemon juice, salt & cracked pepper.
4. Transfer kale to the bowl and massage the juices into it for 1-2 minutes.
5. Lay the kale on the baking tray, along with the cherry tomatoes and place another sheet of baking paper on top.
6. Cook for 20-25 minutes or until kale is crunchy and tomatoes are nice and juicy.
7. Meanwhile, mix together the curry paste, fish sauce and ginger.
8. Rub the paste into the prawns on both sides.
9. Bring a large frying pan to medium heat and cook prawns for 3-4 minutes, making sure you flip them and cook both sides.
10. Transfer kale to a large serving platter and spread prawns out on top.$r$ where name=$r$Crispy Kale & Prawns$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. In a large frying pan, sauté the onion, garlic and red pepper over a medium heat for around 5 minutes, or until the vegetables are tender and beginning to caramelise.
2. Add the turkey to the pan and cook through before adding the spices.
3. Let the spices roast in the pan until they are aromatic before adding the chopped tomatoes, stock, kidney beans and sweet corn.
4. Bring the chilli to the boil and let it reduce for around 30 minutes by which point the sauce will be thick and rich.
5. Season to your taste with a pinch of salt and black pepper before removing from the heat.
6. To serve, top with your favourite Mexican condiments such as guacamole, sour cream or hot sauce.
7. This is a great, nicely balanced dish, however, if you want to lower the carbs substitute the corn and half the beans for some chopped bell peppers.$r$ where name=$r$Turkey Chilli$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Season the salmon fillets with salt and pepper on both sides.
2. Add 25g of the flour to a shallow dish; dredge the salmon in the flour to evenly coat and shake off any excess.
3. Melt 1 tbsp of butter and 1 tbsp oil in a large non-stick pan over medium-high heat.
4. Sear the salmon for 4 minutes on each side or until cooked to your liking.
5. Transfer to a warm plate cover with foil and set aside.
6. Melt the remaining 1 tbsp butter in the pan and sauté the garlic until fragrant.
7. Add the wine and bring to a boil while deglazing the bottom of the pan.
8. Cook until the liquid is almost evaporated, stirring occasionally.
9. Add 80ml of stock to the pan along with the lemon juice, bring to a boil and cook for a further 3 minutes.
10. Whisk the cornstarch together with the reserved stock.
11. Pour the mixture into the pan, stirring through the liquid to create a sauce.
12. Cook until slightly thickened then remove from heat.
13. Stir the capers through the sauce then place the salmon fillets back into the pan, gently turning each fillet to evenly coat in the sauce.
14. Sprinkle with chopped parsley and serve.$r$ where name=$r$Salmon Piccata$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin by soaking the porcini mushrooms in a bowl of boiling water and setting them aside to rehydrate.
2. In a large frying pan, heat the olive oil and gently sauté the chestnut mushrooms.
3. The mushrooms will release a lot of liquid so keep cooking until the liquid has evaporated and the mushrooms are soft and golden brown.
4. Remove the mushrooms from the pan and add the carrots, onion, garlic and celery.
5. Sauté the vegetables for around 10 minutes, or until they have softened, before adding the herbs, celery salt, star anise and tomato purée.
6. Drain the porcini mushrooms and add them to the pan, alongside some of the reserved soaking liquid and the chestnut mushrooms.
7. Combine the ingredients in the pan before adding the chopped tomatoes.
8. Cook the sauce for 30 minutes, by which point it will look luxurious and glossy.
9. Meanwhile, cook the pasta until al dente before draining and mixing through the mushroom sauce.
10. To serve, tear over some fresh basil leaves and enjoy.
11. Top quality fresh porcini are hard to come by.
12. If not perfectly fresh, porcini are frequently prone to spoilage.
13. Hence hy we typically only find the dried variety.$r$ where name=$r$Mushroom Bolognese$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by heating the oil in a large frying pan over medium heat.
2. Add the sausages and cook for 5 minutes, rotating regularly to make sure all sides are cooked.
3. Remove from the pan and set aside.
4. Add the onion to the same pan and cook for 5 minutes or until soft.
5. Stir through the garlic, cumin and parsley.
6. Next, add the tomatoes, kidney beans, chickpeas, corn and 250ml boiling water.
7. Bring to a boil before reducing the heat and simmering for 10 minutes.
8. Place the sausages back in the pan, cover with a lid and cook for another 10 minutes.
9. Serve immediately.$r$ where name=$r$One Pot Vego Sausage Stew$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Add butter to a frying pan and bring to medium heat.
2. Add garlic and rosemary and heat for another 1 minute.
3. Next, add the salmon and cook for 1 minute on each side.
4. Add the wine, reduce the heat to low, cover with a lid and cook for 5 minutes or until the salmon is cooked to your liking.
5. Serve with a simple green salad.$r$ where name=$r$Garlic & Rosemary Salmon$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Firstly, preheat oven to 200c/395f/Gas 6.
2. Wrap the potatoes in foil and bake for 15-20 minutes or until easily pierced with a skewer.
3. Place beef mince, carrot, celery, stock and sun-dried tomato paste in a saucepan and bring to the boil.
4. Reduce heat, cover and cook for 20-25 minutes, stirring regularly.
5. Mix the cornflour with a little water, stir through the beef and cook for 1 more minute.
6. Scoop out the flesh of the potatoes leaving a hole for the filing.
7. Mix potato with beef mixture and then return to potatoes.
8. Season with salt & pepper and garnish with green onions.$r$ where name=$r$Stuffed Potatoes$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Bring 156ml vinegar, 120ml water and 2 tsp honey to a boil in a saucepan.
2. Add the onion and allow to boil for 1 minute.
3. Remove from the heat, and allow to stand for 10 minutes, then drain.
4. Next, pierce the beets a few times with a knife, wrap each beet in a large piece of microwave-safe parchment paper and microwave on high for 7 minutes or until tender.
5. Rub the skin away with a paper towel, cut each beet in half, then into wedges.
6. Combine the remaining 2 tbsp vinegar and 1 tsp honey with the oil, mustard, salt, and pepper in a large bowl.
7. Add beets and kale, tossing to coat.
8. Divide the kale mixture between 4 plates, top each with 85g of salmon, garnish with the onion and almonds and serve.$r$ where name=$r$Kale and Beetroot salad$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by preheating oven to 175c/350f/Gas 4.
2. Place two slices of lemon on each Haddock fillet and wrap in tin foil.
3. Cook for 20 minutes or until fish is cooked through.
4. Bring a frying pan to medium heat and add butter, parsley and garlic.
5. Once the butter has melted add the lemon juice, white wine and chicken stock.
6. Season with salt & cracked pepper and allow to simmer for 5 minutes.
7. Remove from heat and pour into a jug. (making sure you get all of the sauce from the pan) Add olive oil to the same pan and bring to medium heat, again.
8. Add the courgette noodles and cook for 3-4 minutes.
9. Pour the sauce back in the pan, over the courgette noodles and heat through for 2 minutes.
10. Divide courgette noodles on two plates and top with cooked Haddock.$r$ where name=$r$Baked Haddock with Courgette Noodles$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat oven to 200°C/400°F/gas 6.
2. Line 2-3 baking trays with baking paper.
3. Lay the sweet potato on one and the courgette, bell pepper and onion on the others.
4. Drizzle the trays with 2 tsp olive oil and season with salt & cracked pepper.
5. Cook for 30-35 minutes or until tender.
6. Meanwhile, make the dressing by mixing all the ingredients together.
7. Set aside.
8. Rub the tex mex into the tofu.
9. Add the remaining olive oil to a large frying panor grill plate, bring to medium-high heat and add tofu.
10. Cook for 5-7 minutes each side.
11. Divide cooked vegetables on four plates, top with tofu and yoghurt dressing.$r$ where name=$r$Tex Mex Tofu$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by cooking the noodles according to packet instructions.
2. Next, add the olive oil and beef to a large wok and cook for 5-7 minutes.
3. Next, stir through the vegetables.
4. In a small bowl, whisk together all the sauce ingredients until well combined.
5. Pour the sauce over the beef and vegetables and heat through for about 3 minutes.
6. Divide into 3 bowls and top with fresh chilli if you desire.$r$ where name=$r$Easy Chinese Noodles$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Bring a large frying pan to high heat.
2. Add the onion, bacon and vegetable stock and bring to a boil.
3. Reduce the heat and simmer for 10 minutes.
4. Add the kidney beans and thyme and simmer for an additional 5 minutes or until the kidney beans have softened.
5. Divide into 4 bowls and serve with sour cream$r$ where name=$r$Vegetable & Bean Stew$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin by heating the olive oil in a large frying pan.
2. Add the chicken and cook over a medium heat for around 15 minutes until it has cooked through before setting aside.
3. Meanwhile, bring a large saucepan of water to the boil and add the Orzo pasta.
4. Boil the pasta until al dente and drain before returning it to the pot.
5. Add the grated cheese, butter and milk to the pasta and combine until it has formed a smooth and creamy sauce.
6. Stir in the cooked chicken and season to perfection with a pinch of salt and black pepper before serving immediately.
7. Orzo is a rice-shaped pasta that you can cook and serve in much the same way you do rice.
8. That is, you can boil it until the liquid is absorbed, cook it risotto-style, or use the pilaf method.$r$ where name=$r$Cheesy Chicken Orzo$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat oven to 180°C/350°F/Gas 4.
2. Line an oven-proof baking dish with baking paper.
3. Combine the olives, artichoke, bell pepper, and courgette in a large bowl, along with a little liquid from the artichoke hearts, salt & cracked pepper.
4. Toss well to coat and set aside.
5. Place chicken in the baking dish, skin side up, season with oregano and cook for 20 minutes.
6. Remove from the oven, add all the vegetables to the dish (with the chicken still sitting on top) and cook for another 20 minutes or until the chicken is fully cooked.
7. Divide on two plates and top with feta.$r$ where name=$r$Mediterranean Chicken$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin by preheating your oven to 200°C/400°F/gas 6.
2. Toss the potatoes in 2 tablespoons of the oil, season with salt and pepper and roast for around 40 - 45 minutes.
3. In a large frying pan heat the remaining oil, season the turkey steaks and cook for 2-3 minutes each side until cooked through, then set aside.
4. In the same pan add the garlic, capers, stock and lemon juice and allow to simmer for 3-4 minutes.
5. Return the turkey to the pan and allow to warm through.
6. Finally add the dill and lemon zest, stir through then serve with the potatoes and green salad.$r$ where name=$r$Turkey Piccata$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Firstly, bring a pot of salted water to boil, add edamame and peas.
2. Cook for about 4 minutes or until peas are vibrant and bright green.
3. Drain and immediately rinse under cold water before peeling the edamame.
4. Meanwhile, in a small dish, whisk together the lemon zest, lemon juice and olive oil.
5. Assemble the edamame and peas on a serving plate, drizzle lemon dressing on top and toss to combine.
6. Top with torn mint leaves and chunks of Persian fetta.$r$ where name=$r$Edamame & Mint Salad$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Place the meat in the freezer 25-30 minutes before you plan to start cooking, this will make it easier to slice really thinly.
2. Deseed and core the pepper and cut it into very thin strips.
3. Slice the spring onions diagonally and slice the broccoli spears in half lengthways and finally, finely slice the pak choi.
4. Mix together the orange juice, vinegar, soy sauce and chilli sauce and set aside.
5. Carefully slice the beef very thinly.
6. Then, in a bowl, beat the egg white with a fork until slightly frothy Stir in the beef, five-spice powder, cornflour, flour and pepper so everything is evenly coated.
7. Pour 1 tablespoon of the oil into a non-stick wok or frying pan and bring it to a very high heat (test if ready by dropping a small piece of beef in – it should immediately sizzle).
8. Add the beef , stirring so keep the slices separate, and stir-fry for 3-4 minutes.
9. Remove with a slotted spoon and set aside.
10. Steam the broccoli for 1½ minutes, then sit the pak choi on top and steam for another 45 seconds to 1 minute until cooked but still firm.
11. Remove and cool under running cold water to halt the cooking process.
12. Set aside.
13. Pour the remaining oil into the wok and heat it again until very hot.
14. Stir fry the garlic, ginger, red pepper and spring onions for 2-3 minutes until starting to brown.
15. Add the chilli flakes, soy sauce and orange juice mix along with 4-5 tablespoons water.
16. As it comes to a boil, stir in the beef and steamed veg, and cook briefly until warmed through.
17. If you want more sauce you can simply add another 1-2 tablespoons of water.
18. Serve piping hot.$r$ where name=$r$Chinese Chilli Beef$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. the flour, sea salt flakes, Chinese five spice and black to a large bowl and toss to combine. the chicken slices in the flour mix and ensure are well coated. add the oil to a large skillet.
2. Bring the pan to high and once the oil is sizzling, add the chicken and flipping regularly for about 7 minutes. the garlic, spring onion and chillies.
3. Cook for another or until chicken is cooked through and golden. cooked, place chicken on some paper towel to the excess juice, then serve hot. serve with white rice.$r$ where name=$r$Salt & Pepper Chicken$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin by bringing a large pan of water to the boil.
2. Heat a grill pan then toss the courgette strips with the oil and grill them for 2-3 minutes, turning often.
3. Meanwhile, toast the pine nuts over a medium heat in a dry pan.
4. When toasted remove from the pan immediately.
5. Cook the lasagne sheets for 3-4 minutes in the boiling water, then drain well.
6. Carefully slice each sheet in half width ways to make 12 pieces.
7. Next, cook the spinach in 1 tsp water for 2-3 minutes until the leaves have wilted.
8. Drain well, squeezing out the excess moisture with the back of a spoon.
9. Stir the pesto through the cooked courgette strips, then layer with the lasagne sheets, spinach and dollops of the ricotta.
10. Garnish with the basil and pine nuts and serve.$r$ where name=$r$Courgette, spinach and ricotta open lasagne$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. In a medium bowl, combine the beans, sweet corn, salsa, taco seasoning and coriander.
2. Heat a large frying pan over a medium heat and place one tortilla in it.
3. Layer the tortilla with the bean mixture and the cheese before placing a second tortilla on top.
4. Press down on the tortillas firmly before leaving to cook.
5. Once the bottom tortilla has turned golden brown flip the quesadilla and repeat, by which point the cheese filling should have melted.
6. To serve, cut the tortillas into quarters and enjoy with your favourite Mexican condiments such as sour cream, guacamole and hot sauce.
7. Studies have found that a diet high in dietary fibre, especially from bean and legume sources, is protective against mortality due to heart disease, cardiac arrest and stroke.$r$ where name=$r$Black Bean and Corn QuesAdillas$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by cooking rice according to packet instructions.
2. Meanwhile, heat 60ml of water in a large wok.
3. Add vegetables and stir fry for 4-5 minutes.
4. Add the Hoisin sauce and chilli flakes and heat through.
5. Divide rice between 4 bowls, followed by the vegetables.$r$ where name=$r$Easy Asian Stir Fry$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by bringing a pot of salted water to boil.
2. Add the mangetout and cook for 2-3 minutes or until just tender.
3. Drain and rinse under cold water immediately.
4. Meanwhile, add the basil, avocado oil, vinegar, salt & cracked pepper to a blender and blitz until smooth.
5. Toss the tuna with the mangetout, white beans and lettuce.
6. Pour the dressing all over.
7. Divide between two bowls and serve with boiled eggs.$r$ where name=$r$Tuna & Butter Bean Salad$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by heating the olive oil in a deep fry pan.
2. Add the onion and chorizo and cook for 5 minutes.
3. Add the garlic and black olives and cook for another 3-4 minutes.
4. Next, throw in the cherry tomatoes, couscous and stock.
5. Reduce to a low heat, cover, and simmer for 8-10 minutes or until the stock is absorbed.
6. Give it a quick stir every few minutes to make sure it’s not sticking.
7. Serve with lemon wedges.$r$ where name=$r$Spicy Chorizo Couscous$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin by mixing the milk, oats and seasonings together in a large bowl, then add the turkey and mix gently before forming four patties a cm or so thick.
2. Place the patties on an oiled grill pan over medium heat.
3. Grill for 4-5 minutes per side until cooked through.
4. Serve over the kale salad, along with remaining ingredients.$r$ where name=$r$California Burger Bowls$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Heat the oil in a non-stick sauté pan, add the garlic, pepper, chilli and the whites from the spring onions, and fry for 5 mins over a medium-high heat.
2. Meanwhile, put a large pan of water on to boil.
3. Add the spices, tomatoes, most of the coriander and the chickpeas to the sauté pan and cook for 1-2 mins more.
4. Stir in the bouillon powder and enough liquid from the chickpeas to moisten everything, and leave to simmer gently.
5. Once the water is at a rolling boil, crack in your eggs and poach for 2 mins, then remove with a slotted spoon.
6. Stir the spring onion tops into the chickpeas, then very lightly crush a few of the chickpeas with a fork or potato masher to add texture.
7. Spoon the chickpea mixture onto plates, scatter with the reserved coriander and top with the eggs.
8. Serve with an extra sprinkle of cumin for added warmth and flavour if desired$r$ where name=$r$Indian Chickpeas with Poached Eggs$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. In a large bowl, whisk together all the ingredients for the marinade then add the chicken and mix until fully coated.
2. Preheat grill or skillet to medium-high and grease with a little oil.
3. Remove the chicken from the marinade and add to the pan, discarding any leftover marinade.
4. Grill the chicken for 5-8 minutes on each side or until cooked through.
5. Remove from the pan, allow to cool and then slice.
6. Immediately add sliced bell peppers to the same pan.
7. Cook for 3-4 minutes or until they begin to char.
8. Allow everything come to room temperature then begin assembling the ‘bowls’.
9. Assemble 4 airtight containers and add 250 grams of rice to each one, then divide the chicken and bell peppers into each box.
10. Once cooled seal the lids and refrigerate for up to four days.$r$ where name=$r$Chilli Lime Chicken Bowls$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat oven to 200°C/400°F/Gas 6.
2. Melt the butter in a pan, add the onions and flour and cook for about 5 minutes or until the onions have softened.
3. Next, add the butter beans and stock.
4. Simmer for 10 minutes or until the beans have softened.
5. Transfer into an ovenproof casserole dish, sprinkle with cheese, salt & cracked pepper.
6. Place in the oven and cook for 10 minutes or until cheese has melted and turned golden.$r$ where name=$r$Onion and Butter Bean Soup$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. To make the easy Parmesan croutons: Cut the bread into 1cm cubes and toss with 1 tbsp each of olive oil and Parmesan.
2. Heat in a non-stick frying pan over a medium heat until golden brown and crunchy.
3. Set aside to cool.
4. Meanwhile in a small saucepan over medium heat, bring 500ml of water to a boil, and poach the chicken breasts.
5. When cooked remove the chicken from the pan and when cool enough to handle, cut into cubes around 3cm square.
6. Next make the lime dressing.
7. Combine 3 tbsps fresh lime juice, 1 small clove crushed garlic, ¾ tsp salt, ½ tsp grated lime peel and ¼ tsp freshly ground coarse black pepper.
8. Beat in 80ml olive oil until blended.
9. Remove garlic clove just before using.
10. Next, toss the lettuce, cherries, chicken and croutons in a large salad bowl.
11. Dress with the lime dressing, scatter with Parmesan cheese and toss lightly before serving.$r$ where name=$r$Cherry Caesar Salad$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat oven to 190°C/375°F/gas 5.
2. Place the coconut milk, peanut butter and soy sauce in a saucepan over low heat.
3. Cook for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally, allowing the sauce to thicken.
4. Meanwhile, in a large saucepan, add the olive oil and cook the tofu for 7-10 minutes, constantly shaking the pan and flipping the tofu.
5. Transfer the tofu to a baking tray and place in the oven for 5 minutes while you cook the remainder of the meal.
6. Place the bok choy in the same pan the tofu was in and cook for 5 minutes.
7. Transfer to 3 serving bowls, along with the carrot and cucumber.
8. Top with tofu, satay sauce, fresh spring onion and chilli if you desire.$r$ where name=$r$Satay Tofu$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. In a large pot of boiling salted water, cook the linguine until al dente.
2. Meanwhile, melt the butter in a large pan over a medium heat before adding the prawns, garlic and crushed red pepper.
3. Sauté for 3 minutes, or until the prawns have turned pink and the garlic and pepper smell aromatic.
4. Squeeze the lemon juice and pour the wine into the pan and season to perfection.
5. Let the sauce reduce for 5 minutes before removing from the heat and stirring in the pasta, zest and parsley, which will add some freshness to the dish.
6. Mix well before serving immediately with a handful of Parmesan cheese scattered on top.
7. The word linguine means “little tongues” in Italian.$r$ where name=$r$Prawn Linguine$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by preheating oven to 175c/350f/Gas 4.
2. Heat olive oil in a large frying pan.
3. Add onion, garlic paste, courgette, carrot, mushrooms and oregano.
4. Cook for 5 minutes.
5. Add the kidney beans and continue to cook for another 5 minutes.
6. Next, add the Worcestershire sauce, vegetable stock and tinned tomatoes.
7. Allow to simmer for 10-15 minutes while the liquid reduces.
8. Meanwhile, add chopped potatoes to a saucepan and cover with salted water.
9. Bring water to a boil and cook potatoes for 15-20 minutes or until easily pierced with a fork.
10. Once potatoes are cooked, drain, return to the saucepan and mash until smooth.
11. Pour the bean and vegetable mixture into an ovenproof dish and spread mashed potato on top.
12. Sprinkle with cheese and season generously with salt & cracked pepper.
13. Place in the oven and cook for 15-20 minutes or until cheese has melted.$r$ where name=$r$Vegan Cottage Pie$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat oven to 165c/325f/Gas 3.
2. Line a baking tray with baking paper.
3. Cut the stems from the mushrooms and place on the tray and brush with a tsp of oil.
4. Cook mushrooms for 10 minutes.
5. Meanwhile, add the remaining tsp of oil to a frying pan along with onion, garlic and spinach.
6. Cook for 3 minutes before adding the tomatoes and cooking for another 2 minutes.
7. Remove from the heat and stir in breadcrumbs and herbs.
8. Spoon the mixture into the mushrooms, top with vegan cheese, then place them back in the oven to cook for another 10-15 minutes or until the cheese has melted.$r$ where name=$r$Vegan Stuffed Mushrooms$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Using a meat mallet (or a rolling pin) pound out the chicken breasts until they are flat and an even thickness.
2. Sprinkle with salt and pepper.
3. Heat the olive oil in a large pan on a medium/high heat, then cook the chicken breast until golden brown, on both sides then transfer toa plate.
4. Turn the heat down to medium and add the cauliflower, carrot, onion, ginger, cumin, cinnamon, paprika, and Allspice to the pan.
5. Cook, stirring frequently, until the vegetables just begin to soften and the spices are fragrant.
6. Stir in the orange juice, crushed tomatoes and sliced dates.
7. Turn the heat up to high and bring to a boil and cook for a further 2 minutes.
8. Reduce the heat to medium and simmer, stirring frequently for about 5 minutes until the sauce begins to reduce and thicken.
9. Season to taste with salt and pepper.
10. Return the chicken to the pan, nestling it into the vegetables and spooning some sauce over the top.
11. Cover and reduce the heat to medium/low.
12. Cook for a further 10 minutes ensuring the chicken is cooked through.
13. Stir in the coriander and divide the chicken between two plates.
14. Top each dish with the chopped pistachios and place the sliced cucumbers on the side.
15. Garnish with extra coriander, if desired, and enjoy!$r$ where name=$r$Moroccan Chicken Skillet$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Cook the asparagus or green beans and peas for 2-3 min in a large pan of boiling water until just tender. - drain well.
2. Meanwhile, heat the rice according to the packet instructions, then put in a large bowl.
3. Add the asparagus or beans, peas, salmon and spinach.
4. Put the lemon zest and juice, mustard, olive oil and sugar in a bowl and whisk to combine.
5. Drizzle over the rice mixture and gently toss to combine.
6. Serve immediately sprinkled with ground black pepper.$r$ where name=$r$Asparagus, Pea and Salmon Rice$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by cooking the quinoa according to packet instructions.
2. Once cooked, fluff with a fork and set aside.
3. Place the chicken pieces in some plastic wrap and pound to flatten.
4. Then, toss chicken in olive oil.
5. Bring a grill plate to high heat and cook chicken pieces for 4-5 minutes on each side or until fully cooked through.
6. Cover with foil and set aside.
7. Meanwhile, combine all the vegetables in a large bowl.
8. Prepare the dressing by briskly mixing together the buttermilk with goat’s cheese, salt & cracked pepper.
9. Add the quinoa to the vegetables, along with the dressing and toss really well.
10. Transfer to a long serving plate and top with chicken.$r$ where name=$r$Quinoa & Chicken Salad with Buttermilk Dressing$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Cook the penne in a large pan of boiling water, according to the pack instructions until al dente.
2. Meanwhile, blend the basil, parsley, capers, lemon juice and oil ina food processor to make a thick sauce.
3. Drain the pasta well, then return to the pan with the shredded chicken and add the sauce.
4. Toss well, then divide among 4 bowls, sprinkle with black pepper and serve.$r$ where name=$r$Herby Chicken Pasta$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Add the mayonnaise, pickles, spring onion and lemon juice to a small dish and stir well to combine.
2. Set aside.
3. Next, mix together the olive oil, lemon zest, dill, sea salt & cracked pepper in a shallow dish.
4. Submerge the fish fillets and turn to coat both sides.
5. Heat the barbeque or grill plate and cook fish for about 3 minutes each side or until cooked to your liking.
6. Slice buns in half, add a generous dollop of tartaree sauce, a butter lettuce leaf and finally, the fish.$r$ where name=$r$Lemony Fish Burgers$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by cooking pasta according to packet instructions.
2. Drain and set aside.
3. In a large wok or frying pan add the asparagus, courgette and spring onions.
4. Cook for 2 minutes.
5. Add the basil pesto and cook for another 3-4 minutes or until the vegetables are just tender.
6. Toss the spaghetti with vegetables, season with salt & pepper and squeeze the juice of the lemon all over.$r$ where name=$r$Green Spaghetti$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. In a large bowl, mix together the yoghurt, Tandoori paste, lemon juice salt & cracked pepper.
2. Set aside.
3. Pat the chicken thighs dry with some paper towel.
4. Use a sharp knife to make a couple of slices in the thickest part of each thigh. (This will allow the marinade to sink in).
5. Place the chicken in the Tandoori sauce and allow it to marinate in the fridge for at least 1 hour.
6. Preheat the oven to 200c/395f/Gas 6.
7. Line a baking tray with baking paper.
8. Next, heat the grill.
9. Brown the skin of the chicken on each side of each piece for 2-3 minutes.
10. Basting with any extra marinade as you go.
11. Transfer chicken to the baking tray and cook for 10-15 minutes or until the chicken is cooked through and the juices are clear.
12. Once cooked, transfer to a warm dish, cover with foil and let rest for 5-10 minutes before serving.$r$ where name=$r$Tandoori Chicken$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by mixing together the olive oil, garlic and chilli flakes and toss the mushrooms and broccolini to coat.
2. Transfer the vegetables to a large frying pan and cook for 5-6 minutes.
3. Meanwhile, mash the avocado with the lime juice.
4. Divide the vegetables between the tortillas, top with avocado, coriander and chilli sauce.$r$ where name=$r$Shiitake Tacos$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Heat 1 tbsp olive oil in a large frying pan and soften 1 chopped onion for 5 minutes.
2. Add 1 tsp paprika, 1 tsp thyme and the rice, stir for 1 minute, then pour over 3 tbsp sherry or white wine.
3. Once the liquid has evaporated, stir in the tomatoes and stock.
4. Season and continue to cook, uncovered, for about 15 minutes, stirring occasionally until the rice is almost tender and still coated with some liquid.
5. Stir in the seafood and cover with a lid.
6. Simmer for 5 minutes, or until the seafood is cooked through and the rice is now tender.
7. Squeeze over the lemon juice, scatter with parsley and serve with the lemon wedges.$r$ where name=$r$Paella$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Bring a large frying panto high heat and add olive oil.
2. Next, place the salmon steaks in the pan and sprinkle with chilli flakes.
3. Cook for 2-3 minutes each side, or until cooked to your liking.
4. A little undercooked is recommended.
5. Meanwhile, make the dressing by adding all ingredients to a jar and shaking very well to combine.
6. Place cucumber and coriander in a bowl and toss with dressing.
7. Divide salad on 4 plates and place a pieces of chilli salmon on each.$r$ where name=$r$Chilli Salmon$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by cooking the pasta according to packet instructions.
2. Drain and set aside.
3. Meanwhile, bring a frying panto medium heat and add the olive oil, garlic, olives and capers.
4. Cook for about 2 minutes before adding the passata and chilli flakes.
5. Stir through the tuna, breaking up the chunks with your spoon.
6. Add the pasta and continue to stir through.
7. Divide into two bowls and garnish with fresh basil.$r$ where name=$r$Sicilian Pasta$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Add the sesame oil to a large wok and bring to medium- high heat.
2. Add the chicken and cook for 8-10 minutes or until lightly browned and cooked through.
3. Set aside and cover with aluminium foil to keep warm.
4. In the same pan, add the chillies and onion and cook for 5 minutes or until onion is translucent.
5. Next, add the garlic, broccoli, cauliflower, bell pepper and courgette.
6. Cook for 10 minutes or until tender.
7. Meanwhile, mix together the tamari, sesame oil, rice wine vinegar and honey.
8. Once the vegetables are cooked, toss through the cooked chicken and sauce.
9. Heat through for 1-2 minutes.
10. Divide between six bowls and serve with rice or just on it’s own.$r$ where name=$r$Easy Chicken Stir-Fry$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin by preheating your oven to 170°C/325°F/gas 3.
2. Heat 1 teaspoon of the oil in a large heavy-bottomed casserole over a medium to high heat.
3. Cut the lamb into cubes and brown on all sides in two batches for around 3-4 minutes per batch.
4. Transfer to a plate using a slotted spoon.
5. Add another teaspoon of oil to the pan and add the onions, garlic, celery and carrots and fry, stirring, for 3-4 minutes.
6. Add the rosemary and thyme and fry for another minute.
7. Sprinkle over the flour and cook for 2 minutes, stirring constantly to cook the flour.
8. Return the lamb to the pan, pour over the stock and stir in the Worcestershire sauce and tomato purée, then bring to the boil.
9. Layer the potatoes on top in two overlapping layers, seasoning between the layers.
10. Cover with the lid and bake in the oven for 1/2 hours, or until the lamb and the potatoes are tender.
11. Remove the lid and increase the oven temperature to 200°C/400°F/gas 6.
12. Brush the potatoes with the final teaspoon of oil and bake for a further 15 minutes, or until the top is nicely browned and crispy.$r$ where name=$r$Lamb Hotpot$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by cooking pasta according to packet instructions.
2. Heat oven to 200°C/400°F/gas 6 and line a baking tray with baking paper.
3. Lay prosciutto on the tray and cook for 10-15 minutes or until crispy.
4. In a medium sized skillet, add the garlic, cream and lime juice.
5. Heat for 3-5 minutes on medium heat, stirring continuously.
6. Add the pasta and stir to heat through.
7. Finally, add the parsley and season with salt & cracked pepper.
8. Divide into four bowls and serve immediately.$r$ where name=$r$Crunchy Prosciutto Pasta$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin by preheating your grill to a medium heat.
2. Place the tortillas under the grill for around 1 minute, or until they are lightly toasted all over – remember to watch the tortillas carefully as they will burn very easily.
3. Once cooked, remove from the grill and set aside.
4. To soften the onion, gently sauté in a pan for 5 minutes or, alternatively, cook them in a microwave for 2 minutes.
5. While the onion cooks, add the shredded chicken to a bowl and combine with the barbeque sauce and balsamic vinegar.
6. To assemble the pizza, spread the tortillas with barbeque sauce and scatter over the chicken, onions and tomatoes.
7. Top with the grated mozzarella and Parmesan before placing the pizza under the grill once again.
8. Once the cheese has melted and is beginning to brown, remove the pizza from the oven and serve.
9. Everyone loves a pizza, by switching your often grease ladened dough for a tortilla wrap you trim the calories and add some crunch.
10. Try it with your favourite toppings.$r$ where name=$r$BBQ Chicken Tortilla Pizza$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Bring a large frying pan to high heat, add the oil and brown the chicken for about 3-4 minutes.
2. Transfer to a 5.5L slow cooker.
3. Add onion to the same pan and cook for about 5 minutes or until translucent.
4. Add the garlic, apricot nectar, balsamic vinegar, parsley and thyme.
5. Pour the mixture into the slow cooker, cover and cook on low for 6 hours.
6. Add the apricot halves for the last 30 minutes.
7. Optional: serve with brown rice or couscous.$r$ where name=$r$Slow Cooker Apricot Chicken$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Mix the flour, salt & cracked pepper and rosemary together in a large bowl and coat the lamb.
2. Add the chopped vegetables and lamb to a very deep casserole dish. (Make sure you layer the vegetables and the meat all the way up, with a vegetable layer last).
3. Fill the pot with enough water to just cover the top layer.
4. Add the Worcestershire sauce.
5. Bring to a boil, cover and then reduce the heat to a simmer.
6. Cook for approximately 1 1/2 hours or until the water has reduced, vegetables are tender and meat is cooked.
7. Divide into four bowls and serve with crusty bread, optional.$r$ where name=$r$Lamb Stew$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Cook the pasta according to package directions.
2. Drain and reserve 120ml of the cooking water.
3. Return to the pan and cover to keep warm.
4. While pasta is cooking, pat the prawns dry with paper towels then season with pepper and ¼ tsp of salt.
5. Heat half of the olive oil in a large non-stick pan over a high heat.
6. Cook the prawns, stirring often, until cooked through.
7. Transfer to a plate and cover to keep warm.
8. In the same pan reduce heat to medium-high, add the leek, garlic, remaining oil, and remaining ½ tsp of salt.
9. Cook, stirring often, until the leek is slightly tender.
10. Next add the peas, cream, lemon zest, lemon juice, and reserved pasta cooking liquid.
11. Reduce to a simmer and continue to cook until sauce thickens, then add the prawns and toss to coat.
12. Divide the pasta evenly among 4 bowls, top with the prawns and sauce.
13. Sprinkle with dill and serve immediately.$r$ where name=$r$Prawn and Leek Spaghetti$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by draining as much water out of the grated potato as you can.
2. Transfer to a large bowl, add the egg, spring onion, salt & cracked pepper, mix to combine.
3. Bring a large frying pan to medium heat and add olive oil.
4. Spoon half the mixture into a pancake shape into the pan.
5. Cook for about 5 minutes each side or until the potato has turned golden.
6. Set aside and cook the remainder of the potato.
7. Add the teriyaki sauce to the same pan and heat on low.
8. Place the pancakes gently back into the pan and coat in the sauce.
9. Remove from the pan, divide on two plates and drizzle with Kewpie mayonnaise and extra spring onions.$r$ where name=$r$Okonomiyaki$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat oven to 200°C/400°F/gas 6.
2. Slice very thin slices in the lamb racks.
3. In a medium bowl, mix together the red wine vinegar, rosemary and sea salt.
4. Submerge the lamb racks in the sauce with the fatty side down.
5. Let it sit for 20 minutes.
6. Meanwhile, toss the Brussels sprouts in olive oil, garlic, salt & cracked pepper.
7. Transfer the lamb and Brussels sprouts to an ovenproof dish and cook for 25 minutes or until the lamb is cooked to your liking. (keep the leftover marinade and set aside) Give the pan a shake half way through to make sure the Brussels sprouts don’t stick.
8. Meanwhile add the reserved sauce to a small saucepan and bring to a boil.
9. Cook for 2-3 minutes or until thickened.
10. Divide the lamb and Brussels sprouts between two plates and serve with sauce.$r$ where name=$r$Lamb Racks with Sprouts$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by cooking the noodles according to packet instructions.
2. Drain and set aside.
3. Next, add the peanut oil to a large wok and bring it to a medium-high heat.
4. Add the pork mince and cook for 5-7 minutes or until cooked through.
5. Mix together the fish sauce, lime juice and coconut sugar in a small bowl, then pour it over the pork.
6. Stir to heat through.
7. Toss the pork with the cooked noodles, shredded carrot, mint leaves and coriander.$r$ where name=$r$Vietnamese Pork Noodles$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by cooking the pasta according to packet instructions.
2. Meanwhile, heat the oil in a large frying pan on medium- high heat.
3. Add the onion and cook for 5 minutes.
4. Add all the other ingredients and cook, stirring regularly for 7-10 minutes.
5. Divide pasta between four bowls, top with bolognese sauce and sprinkle with nutritional yeast flakes.$r$ where name=$r$Vegan Bolognese$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Bring the broth to a boil in a medium sized heavy pot, add the quinoa, lower the heat and cook, covered with a lid, for 25 minutes.
2. Remove from the heat and set aside, still covered, for 5 minutes, then fluff with a fork.
3. While the quinoa cooks, add 2 tsp of the olive oil, half of the lemon juice and zest, oregano, parsley, garlic, chilli, salt and pepper to a small bowl and mix well.
4. Add the prawns and toss well to coat.
5. Heat a griddle or heavy frying pan over a high heat.
6. When hot, spray with cooking oil, add the prawns and cook for 2 to 3 minutes on each side.
7. Divide the salad leaves amongst 4 large serving bowls on one half of the dish, add half the quinoa to the other side, then top with prawn, avocado, tomato, and onion.
8. Dress with the remaining olive oil, salt, pepper, red chilli flakes and drizzle with lemon juice.
9. Serve immediately.$r$ where name=$r$LEMON-CHILLI PRAWN QUINOA BOWLS$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Set aside 2 tbsp of the onion for the salsa, then cook the remaining onion and half the pepper in the oil for 4 minutes or until softened and coloured.
2. Next stir in the rice, then add in the stock.
3. Then add the kidney beans and a pinch of salt.
4. Bring the pan to a boil, stir, cover, then reduce the heat to a simmer.
5. Cook for 15 minutes or until the rice is tender and the liquid absorbed.
6. Dust the turkey steaks with the Cajun spice and griddle or fry them in a non-stick pan for about 4-6 minutes on each side until cooked through.
7. Cut the pineapple into small pieces and mix with the reserved red onion, pepper, green chilli and lime juice.
8. Spoon some salsa over each steak and serve with the rice.$r$ where name=$r$Cajun turkey steaks with pineapple salsa$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Add the salad ingredients to a medium-sized bowl and toss to combine.
2. Add the dressing ingredients to a jar and shake very well to combine.
3. Pour the dressing over the salad and set aside.
4. Next, mix the bread crumbs, parmesan cheese and lemon rind together in a medium sized bowl.
5. In a separate bowl, whisk together the egg and dijon.
6. Dip the veal cutlets in the egg, followed by the breadcrumb mix.
7. Next, add the olive oil to large frying panand bring it to medium-high heat.
8. Place the cutlets in the pan and cook for about 3 minutes each side.
9. Serve immediately alongside radicchio salad.$r$ where name=$r$Parmesan Crusted Veal Cutlets$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by mixing the olive oil, lemon juice, salt & cracked pepper.
2. Set aside.
3. Next, wash the bulgar wheat and soak it in water for 6 minutes.
4. Make sure you drain it really well and squeeze out any excess water.
5. Pour the bulgar wheat into the bowl with the lemon dressing so it can soak in the flavour.
6. Once you’ve chopped all the vegetables and herbs, transfer them, along with the tuna to the bowl with the bulgar wheat and toss really well to combine.
7. Refrigerate for 30 minutes before serving.$r$ where name=$r$Tuna Tabbouleh$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Slice the chorizo and fry gently in a large saucepan over a medium heat for 5 minutes or until it begins to turn a dark brown.
2. Add the tomatoes and butter beans, bring to the boil, then simmer for 10 minutes.
3. Stir through the tub of pesto, season to your liking, divide among 4 bowls and serve.$r$ where name=$r$Butter bean & chorizo stew$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat oven to 200°C/400°F/gas 6.
2. Line a baking tray with baking paper.
3. Toss the sweet potato, beetroot and onion in 1 tsp olive oil and chilli flakes and cook for 25-30 minutes.
4. Add the remaining olive oil to a wok and cook kale for 5-7 minutes.
5. Meanwhile, make the sauce by whisking together the tahini, water and honey.
6. Transfer vegetables to a serving bowl, top with cashews and drizzle with sauce.$r$ where name=$r$Vegan Buddha Bowl$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Firstly, make the peanut sauce by adding all ingredients to a blender or food processor and blending until smooth.
2. Add canola oil to a large frying pan and bring to a medium heat.
3. Add tofu and cook for about 10-12 minutes.
4. Flipping 2-3 times.
5. Add the peanut sauce and gently stir to coat the tofu pieces.
6. Cook for another 4-5 minutes, then remove from the heat.
7. Fill the lettuce leaves with the tofu mixture and top with chopped peanuts and fresh coriander.$r$ where name=$r$Crispy Tofu Cups$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat oven to 180°C/350°F/gas 5 and line a baking tray with baking paper.
2. Toss the pumpkin in olive oil and sumac, lay evenly on the baking tray and cook for 15 minutes (or until just beginning to soften but not fully cooked yet).
3. Next, spread onion relish all over the 2 flat breads.
4. Top with cooked pumpkin and goat’s cheese and cook for 20 minutes or until goat’s cheese is melting.
5. Once cooked, top with baby spinach and season with salt & cracked pepper.$r$ where name=$r$Pumpkin & Goat’s Cheese Flat Breads$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin by preheating your oven to 230°C/450°F/gas 8.
2. Arrange the salmon fillets skinned side down, on a non-stick baking tray.
3. Spread each fillet with some pesto, combine the breadcrumbs and cheese together and sprinkle over.
4. Drizzle each fillet with some olive oil and bake for 10 minutes.
5. Boil the green beans for 3-4 minutes until tender and crisp.
6. Drain well, toss in a little olive oil, season to taste with salt and pepper and serve with the salmon$r$ where name=$r$Salmon with Pesto Crust$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by preheating the oven to 200°C/400°F/gas 6.
2. Line a baking tray with baking paper.
3. Toss the potato and bell pepper in 2 tsp olive oil and lay the vegetables across.
4. Cook for 30 minutes or until the potatoes are golden and the bell pepper is soft.
5. Meanwhile, bring a medium-sized frying panto medium heat, add 1 tsp olive oil and cook onions for 5 minutes.
6. Add the balsamic vinegar and 1 tbsp of water and cook for another 5 minutes or until sticky, stirring constantly.
7. Rub the remaining oil and garlic into the pork steaks.
8. Bring a frying panto medium-high heat and cook steaks for 3-4 minutes each side.
9. Once cooked, set aside under some tin foil.
10. Toss the cooked potato and bell pepper with spinach and divide on two plates.
11. Top with sliced pork and caramelised onion.$r$ where name=$r$Pork with Caramelised Onion$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by seasoning the steaks with salt & cracked pepper.
2. Next bring a large frying panto high heat.
3. Once the pan is very hot, add half the butter, oil and garlic.
4. Once it’s beginning to brown, place four of the steaks in the pan.
5. Cook for 30 seconds each side.
