5. If you decide not to add in protein powder, simply replace with about 3 more tablespoons of cocoa powder or until batter tastes chocolatey enough to your liking.
6. Place the truffle batter in the fridge for about 20 minutes.
7. Once chilled remove from the fridge and form the batter into 12 even dough balls; roll them with your hands to form a ball (you can use latex gloves if you don’t want messy hands) Place the formed truffles on a baking tray lined with parchment paper and place back in fridge while you prepare the chocolate coating: Heat the chocolate and 1 teaspoon coconut oil in small saucepan on very low.
8. Stir every so often until chocolate has melted and is smooth.
9. Remove from heat.
10. Lift each truffle with a fork or toothpick and dip into the chocolate mixture to coat - they don’t have to be perfect!
11. Roll in sprinkles, nuts or coconut if desired.
12. Place back on parchment paper and return to the fridge for ten minutes.
13. Once chilled, enjoy these delicious sweet treats!$r$ where name=$r$Black Bean Chocolate Protein Truffles$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. 25g rolled oats (gluten free if required) Firstly, preheat oven to 177°C/350°F/Gas 4.
2. Spray 8x8 inch baking 50g unsweetened cocoa powder pan with nonstick cooking spray.
3. 55g whey chocolate protein powder Place oats in a blender and blend for one minute or until they 120ml unsweetened applesauce resemble the consistency of flour.
4. Transfer oat flour to a medium tegg bowl then whisk in cocoa powder and protein powder, set aside ‘ tbsp honey Whisk together applesauce, egg, honey, vanilla and almond milk (tsp vanilla extract until smooth and well combined.
5. Add to dry ingredients and mix 160ml almond milk, unsweetened together until just combined.
6. 45q chocolate chips, plus 2 tbsp for topping Next, heat coconut oil and the chocolate chips (save 2 tbsp) in 65g raspberries, broken up into large pieces a small saucepan over very low heat.
7. Stir continuously until all chocolate chips and coconut oil have melted together. (You can also heat them in a microwave safe bowl for 30-45 seconds.) Gently stir into brownie batter.
8. Pour mixture into prepared pan.
9. Sprinkle remaining 2 tbsp of chocolate chips and raspberries on top and bake for 18-22 minutes or until just cooked through and the top has set.
10. Transfer pan to wire rack to cool completely.
11. Once cool, cut into 12 bars.
