3. Use a rubber spatula to break the dough up a bit, then add the chocolate chips and pulse a couple of times, making sure the chips evenly dispersed in the dough.
4. Remove the dough from the processor then (using a generous ½ tbsp amount), roll into balls and place on a small parchment paper-lined baking sheet.
5. Place in the fridge to chill for 10-15 minutes.
6. Meanwhile make the coating.
