3. Place the lid on and cook for another 4-5 minutes.
4. Remove from the pan and set aside under some aluminium foil.
5. Add the spinach to the same pan and cook for 2-3 minutes or until wilted and cooked through.
6. Transfer the eggs and spinach to your serving plate and sprinkle with parmesan cheese, salt & cracked pepper.$r$ where name=$r$Sauteed Spinach & Eggs$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin by warming the stock.
2. Put the couscous in a large bowl and pour over the hot stock, cover with cling film and put to one side for 10 minutes. couscous with a fork.
3. Stir in the spring onions, herbs, pomegranate seeds, lemon juice and olive oil.
4. Serve piping hot.$r$ where name=$r$Pomegranate and herb couscous$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat oven to 200c/395f/Gas 6.
2. Line a baking tray with baking paper and spread mini filo pastry cups out on the tray evenly.
3. Mix ham, sausage, bacon, onion and cheese together and divide evenly into the filo cups.
4. Next, crack your eggs into a small bowl, add milk, parsley salt & cracked pepper and whisk.
5. Pour the whisked egg mixture into the filo cups.
6. Place in the oven and cook for about 8 minutes or until the egg is fully cooked.$r$ where name=$r$Three Pork Quiches$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Pour the coconut milk, water, and salt into a medium-sized saucepan and bring to a boil.
2. Pour the couscous into the mixture, remove from the heat, cover with a lid, and set aside for 5 minutes. up with a fork and serve.
3. This works well as a side dish or with vegetables, meat or fish for a main dish.$r$ where name=$r$Coconut Couscous$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Add all ingredients to your food processor or blender and blend for 1 minutes.
2. Scrape down the sides so everything is touching the blades and blend for an additional 1 minutes.
3. Sprinkle with sea salt flakes.$r$ where name=$r$Coconut Cashew Butter$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin by preheating your oven to 180°C/350°F/gas 4 Top each pita evenly with spaghetti sauce, then a layer of basil, mozzarella, onion, and bell pepper.
2. Arrange the topped pitas on lined baking sheet.
3. Bake in the oven for 10 to 12 minutes, or until cheese is melted and bubbling Serve piping hot$r$ where name=$r$Pita Pizza (v)$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat oven to 200°C/400°F/Gas 6.
2. Line a baking tray with baking paper and cook bacon for 20-25 minutes or until very crispy.
3. Once cooked, transfer to a plate lined with paper towel to allow some of the oil to absorb.
4. In a small bowl, mix together the sherry vinegar, olive oil and Dijon mustard.
5. Meanwhile, in a medium sized frying pan, add the tsp of olive oil and halloumi and cook on medium-high heat for 2 minutes on each side.
6. Arrange tomatoes on a large plate, toss with sherry dressing and top with halloumi and chives.$r$ where name=$r$Bacon & Tomato Salad$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Bring a large pot of salted water to boil and cook spinach for about 30 seconds.
2. Drain and place in a bowl of iced water to cool it down.
3. Once cold, drain and use your hands to squeeze out as much excess water from the spinach as you can.
4. Bring a medium-large frying pan to medium heat, add butter and onion and cook for 3-4 minutes or until onion is soft.
5. Add the garlic and heat for another 1 minute before adding milk, cream, flour, nutmeg, salt & cracked pepper.
6. Once thickened slightly, add the spinach and parmesan and stir to combine.
7. Feel free to add extra parmesan when serving.$r$ where name=$r$Creamy Spinach$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Add all ingredients to a food processor or blender and blend for 1-2 minutes or until smooth and creamy.
2. Serve with chopped carrot, celery and cucumber sticks or pitta bread.$r$ where name=$r$Homemade Hummus$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Begin by preheating your oven to 180°C/350°F/gas 4 and line a baking tray with non-stick paper.
2. Mix the peanut butter, garlic, curry powder, a few drops of soy sauce and lime juice in a bowl.
3. Some peanut butters are thicker than others, so add a dash of boiling water to get a coating consistency if required Add the chicken and coat well.
4. Arrange on the baking sheet, spaced apart, and bake for around 8-10 minutes until cooked, but still moist.
5. Serve warm with the cucumber fingers, and sweet chilli sauce.
6. Alternatively, allow to cool and the chicken will keep in the fridge for up to 2 days.$r$ where name=$r$Chicken Satay Strips$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat oven to 200°C/400°F/gas 6 and line a baking tray with baking paper.
2. Trim the stalk of the cauliflower and any leaves.
3. Cut the cauliflower lengthways down the middle.
4. Brush well with olive oil on both sides and season with salt & cracked pepper.
5. Cook for 10 minutes, flip and continue to cook for another 5 minutes.
6. Remove from the oven, brush with pesto, top with mozzarella and cook for another 5 minutes or until cheese is melting.
7. Serve hot.$r$ where name=$r$Sundried Tomato Cauliflower Steaks$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by heating the oil in a non-stick skillet.
2. Add the onion and cook for 5 minutes or until nice and soft.
3. Next, add the garlic and taco seasoning and stir to coat the onion for 1 minute.
4. Add the beans and water and cook, stirring occasionally for 5-7 minutes or until the water has evaporated.
5. Transfer the bean mix to a food processor or blender, add the lime juice and blitz until smooth.
6. Serve with corn chips.$r$ where name=$r$3POINTS$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Combine the chilli flakes, Chinese five spice, garlic, salt & cracked pepper and rice flour together in a large shallow dish.
2. Submerge the tofu in the flour and spices, making sure all edges are well coated.
3. Add the vegetable oil to a large frying pan and bring it to a medium-low heat.
4. Add the tofu and cook for 2-3 minutes each side or until golden and a little crispy.
5. Sprinkle with sesame seeds and serve hot.$r$ where name=$r$Salt & Pepper Tofu$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Pre-heat a large heavy frying pan over medium -high heat.
2. Meanwhile, in a large bowl toss the cubed bread in half the olive oil.
3. Add bread to the pan and toast for around 10 minutes until it appears golden and crisp.
4. Set aside on kitchen paper to cool.
5. In a small bowl, whisk together the dressing ingredients: red wine vinegar, remaining olive oil and honey.
6. Season with salt and pepper.
7. Add the bread, cucumber, tomatoes, onion and garlic together in a large bowl.
8. Toss with dressing until evenly coated and season with more salt and pepper to your liking.
9. Garnish with basil and serve.$r$ where name=$r$Panzanella$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Firstly, use a food processor or manually grate the courgette into a large bowl.
2. Add all other ingredients (except olive oil) and mix to combine.
3. Bring a frying pan to medium heat and add a little olive oil.
4. Cook cakes 2-3 at a time. (use a spoon to transfer batter to the pan and flatten each one with the back of the spoon).
5. When one batch is cooked, set aside under some foil to keep warm.
6. Cook for 3-4 minutes before gently flipping with a spatula and cooking for another 3-4 minutes.
7. Transfer to serving plates, top with feta and extra fresh parsley.$r$ where name=$r$Courgette Cakes$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Place the chickpeas, flour, parmesan cheese, parsley, salt and pepper in a bowl, along with 2 tbsp water.
2. Mash until fully combined.
3. Next, heat the oil in a large skillet.
4. Allow to the oil to get nice and hot before adding the fritters.
5. Divide mixture into six patties and cook each one for 2-3 minutes each side or until cooked through and golden.
6. Set aside on some kitchen towel and serve with a little relish or mayonnaise.$r$ where name=$r$Chickpea Fritters$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Start by preheating the oven to 200°C/400°F/ gas 6.
2. Add the beef, garlic, oregano, salt & pepper, chilli paste, parmesan cheese, bread crumbs, egg and milk to a large bowl and mix well to combine.
3. Roll the mixture into 15-20 balls.
4. Next, heat the oil in a large frying panand cook the meatballs for 3-4 minutes.
5. All you’re doing for now is browning the outside, as they will continue to cook in the oven.
6. Add a few spoonfuls of passata to the bottom of an oven- proof casserole dish.
7. Then, lay the meatballs in the dish.
8. Pour the rest of the sauce all over, top with mozzarella and sprinkle with a little extra oregano, salt & cracked pepper.
9. Cover with foil and cook for 30 minutes or until cheese has melted and sauce is bubbling.
10. Serve hot!$r$ where name=$r$Cheesy Meatballs$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Mix the tuna, mayonnaise, capers and Dijon mustard together in a small bowl.
2. Spread one slice of bread with tuna mix and top with the other slice.
3. Place in the toasted sandwich maker and cook until golden and toasted.$r$ where name=$r$Grilled Tuna Sandwich$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat the oven to 200°C/400°F/gas 6.
2. Line a baking tray with baking paper.
3. Start by preparing three medium sized bowls.
4. Add flour, ground coriander and salt to the first and toss to combine.
5. In the second bowl, crack the eggs and whisk well.
6. In the third bowl, add the breadcrumbs and almonds.
7. Submerge the salmon pieces in the flour, dip them in the egg mix, and finally roll them in the bread crumb/almond mix.
8. Lay the salmon bites on the baking tray and cook for 10-12 minutes or until golden.
9. Serve with sweet chilli sauce.$r$ where name=$r$Salmon Bites$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Add the parsley, basil and garlic to a food processor, and blitz until the leaves are chopped into small, fine pieces.
2. Add the olive oil and lime juice while the motor is still running.
3. Season with salt & cracked pepper and blitz one last time.
4. Set aside.
5. Toss the steak in olive oil and dried parsley and thread pieces onto individual skewers.
6. Bring a grill plate to medium high heat and cook the skewers for 2-3 minutes each side or until cooked to your liking.
7. Drizzle salsa verde all over the skewers and serve hot.$r$ where name=$r$Beef Skewers with Salsa Verde$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Preheat oven to 200c/395f/Gas 6.
2. Line a baking tray with foil, place bacon rashers on the tray and cook for 15-20 minutes or until crispy.
3. Place potatoes in a large pot of salted water.
4. Bring to a boil and cook for 15-18 minutes, or until the potatoes have softened and can be easily pierced with a fork.
5. Meanwhile, melt butter with milk, either in the microwave or on the stove.
6. Once cooked, drain, return to the pot and mash.
7. Pour butter and milk over the potatoes and stir through until nice and creamy.
8. Season well with salt & cracked pepper.
9. In a separate bowl, mash avocado with garlic and chilli flakes.
10. Top potato with avocado mash, crumbled bacon and spring onions.$r$ where name=$r$Loaded Mashed Potato$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
update public.recipes set method=$r$1. Mix together the olive oil, lemon juice, lemon zest, basil and honey.
2. Submerge the prawns in the marinade, cover and refrigerate for 4-5 hours.
3. Meanwhile, toss together the red onion and cherry tomatoes.
4. Bring a bbq grill plate to high heat and cook the prawns for 2-3 minutes each side.
5. Toss the prawns with the onion and cherry tomatoes.
6. Serve with lemon wedges.$r$ where name=$r$4POINTS$r$ and image_url not like $x$%abook-%$x$;
